d 'MINVAR': module to conduct longitudinal measurement invariance tests
d
d   minvar tests whether a latent construct is measured
d equivalently across repeated measurements (or any set of parallel
d    indicator lists in wide format).  It fits a sequence of nested
d models and compares them:	  configural	  same items load
d on the same factor at each timepoint; all loadings and intercepts
d free	     weak (metric)   loadings constrained equal across
d timepoints	   strong (scalar) loadings and intercepts
d constrained equal across timepoints	    strict (residual)	   
d		    optional fourth step (the strict option): each
d item's residual variance also equated across timepoints    There
d is no limit on the number of indicators, and up to 16
d timepoints/groups are accepted. Effects coding is used for   
d identification (Little, Slegers, & Card 2006): each factor's
d loadings sum to the number of indicators and its intercepts sum  
d  to 0, so the latent variables keep the metric of the items and
d factor means are estimated at every timepoint. The residual of   
d each item is allowed to covary with the residual of the same item
d at every other timepoint. Estimation is by method(mlmv)   
d (full-information ML under missing data) unless overridden. 
d
d KW: measurement invariance
d KW: longitudinal data
d
d Requires: Stata version 
d
d Distribution-Date: 20260830
d
d Author: W. Justin Dyer,  Brigham Young University
d Support: email Justin.Dyer@@byu.edu
d
f minvar.ado
